# SocratiCode index exclusions (#240) — gitignore syntax, layered on top of
# SocratiCode's built-in defaults and .gitignore.
#
# Vendored skill trees are agent instructions, not project code. Indexing them
# inflates embedding time and lets vendor prose outrank this repo's own code in
# codebase_search results.
#
# `skills/` itself is NOT excluded. Since #413 it holds no first-party skill:
# every entry is a symlink into skills-vendor/ and indexes under that real path,
# so excluding skills-vendor/ already covers them. A first-party skill added
# there later would be indexed, which is what it would want.
skills-vendor/
.claude/skills/

# Dated prose (#300). docs/plans/ is registered as the `design-and-plans`
# context artifact, so it stays searchable through codebase_context_search
# (artifactName "design-and-plans"); left here, superseded plans outranked the
# code that replaced them in codebase_search. Measured case: docs/SOCRATICODE.md
# → Repo-specific notes → Index scope here.
docs/plans/
